From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): localise defect A to the V side and rule out
 seven causes

Splitting the two sides of the cache on the pristine PrismML build, SC117,
head_dim 256:

  q8_0 K + f16 V  -> 7.3955   fine
  f16 K + q8_0 V  -> 92.5372  broken
  q8_0 K + q4_0 V -> 7.4975   fine
  q4_0 K + q8_0 V -> 88.6076  broken

Whenever V is q8_0 the result is garbage and the K type is irrelevant, which is a
much sharper statement than "q8_0 KV is broken" and matches the kernels: K is
consumed by a dot product against its quantized form, V is dequantised first.

Seven causes eliminated, each by measurement:

  * PrismML's KV mean-centering - the cpy_k() hook is guarded by a k_bar that is
    only filled when --kv-mean-center is passed, and it never was.
  * the attention rotation - LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1 moves the number but fixes
    nothing, and leaves the control healthy.
  * HIP CUDA graphs, the one compile-time difference between the two builds -
    GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1 gives byte-identical numbers, so perplexity does not
    exercise that path. Still worth aligning the option.
  * their convert.cu (+117) and dequantize.cuh (+29) edits - private types only, no
    q8_0 line at all.
  * a missing upstream FA fix - 3 commits to fattn-vec.cuh in the whole range, none
    about quantized V.
  * the FA kernel at head_dim 128 - zero test-backend-ops failures there.
  * the TurboQuant port - reproduces without any TurboQuant code.

Next is a build-level bisect from the merge-base. git worktree add hangs on the
whole-tree checkout here, so it has to be exported with git archive instead. Also
recorded the hard way: do NOT run git worktree prune in this environment, it
deleted the whole .git/worktrees/ directory and dropped both fusion worktree
registrations (all data intact, restored by hand).
