+## 2026-09-19 (final): defect A localised to the V side, seven causes ruled out
+
+Chasing defect A on the pristine PrismML build (SC117, head_dim 256,
+`-c 512 -fa 1 --chunks 8 -ngl 999`, corpus wiki.test.raw).
+
+### It is the V cache, not the K cache
+
+Splitting the two sides of the cache:
+
+| K | V | PPL | |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| q8_0 | f16 | 7.3955 | fine |
+| f16 | q8_0 | **92.5372** | broken |
+| q8_0 | q4_0 | 7.4975 | fine |
+| q4_0 | q8_0 | **88.6076** | broken |
+
+**Whenever V is q8_0 the result is garbage; the K type is irrelevant.** That is a
+much sharper statement than "q8_0 KV is broken", and it lines up with how the
+attention kernels work: K is consumed by a dot product against its quantized form,
+while V is dequantised first.
+
+### Ruled out, each by measurement rather than reasoning
+
+1. **PrismML's KV mean-centering** (`7fb3d5b`, `36d1dee`) - the only fork-specific
+   KV surgery in the tree, so the obvious suspect. The `cpy_k()` hook is guarded by
+   `if (!k_bar.empty() && k_bar[ikv] != nullptr)`, `k_bar` is filled only by
+   `load_kv_mean_center()`, and that runs only when `--kv-mean-center` is passed. It
+   was never passed, so it is dead code for these runs.
+2. **The attention rotation** (`attn_rot_k` / `attn_rot_v`, auto-enabled whenever the
+   cache type is quantized). `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1` leaves q8_0 broken
+   (92.2627 -> 104.8927: the number moves, so the switch works, but nothing is fixed)
+   and leaves the control healthy (llama.cpp base, q8_0 at head_dim 128:
+   10.7160 -> 10.6632).
+3. **HIP CUDA graphs**, the one compile-time option where the two builds differ
+   (PrismML `GGML_HIP_GRAPHS=ON`, llama.cpp fusion `OFF`). Disabling at run time with
+   `GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1` gives **byte-identical** numbers, including for the
+   f16 control, so perplexity does not exercise the graph path and this option cannot
+   explain the difference. Still worth aligning between the two builds.
+4. **PrismML's own edits to `convert.cu`** (+117 lines) and **`dequantize.cuh`**
+   (+29 lines): both only add their private types (PQ2_0, PTQ1_0, Q2_0_g128) and
+   contain **no q8_0 line at all**.
+5. **A missing upstream fix in the FA files.** Between the merge-base and b11046,
+   `fattn-vec.cuh` saw 3 commits, `fattn-common.cuh` 2, and `set-rows.cu`, `cpy.cu`
+   and `dequantize.cuh` none - none about quantized V.
+6. **The FA kernel itself** at head_dim 128 (test-backend-ops: zero failures there).
+7. **The TurboQuant port** - this reproduces on a build with no TurboQuant code.
+
+### Where that leaves it
+
+A bug in PrismML's base specific to `q8_0` used as the **V** cache type, at any head
+size, with `q4_0` and `f16` as working controls. Everything the two sides share is
+now excluded, and the fault is not in any file PrismML touched with an obvious q8_0
+suspect.
+
+The next step is a build-level bisect, which needs a build of the merge-base
+(`5ea87ddad`). That was attempted with `git worktree add` and **hung** - the
+whole-tree-checkout pathology this project recorded on 2026-09-15. Use
+`git archive 5ea87ddad | tar -x` into a plain directory instead, then bisect:
+
+* if the merge-base is also broken, the regression is upstream's and the fix sits
+  somewhere in the 430 commits this base lacks;
+* if the merge-base is clean, bisect PrismML's 93 own commits (roughly 7 build cycles).
+
+**Do not run `git worktree prune` in this environment.** It deleted
+`<LLAMA_SRC>/llama.cpp/.git/worktrees/` outright and dropped both fusion
+worktree registrations - `git worktree list` afterwards showed only the main
+checkout. The directories, branches and commits were all intact and were restored by
+re-creating `gitdir` / `HEAD` / `commondir` under `.git/worktrees/<name>` by hand,
+plus a `git reset` to rebuild the index. `git worktree repair` cannot help: it needs
+the admin entry in order to locate the repository, which is exactly what is gone.
+Script: `temp_clean_later/scripts/restore-worktree-admin.py`.
